      "claim": "Drug users or persons with drug-related criminal histories do not constitute a suspect or quasi-suspect class under the Equal Protection Clause.",
      "evidence": "U.S. Supreme Court precedent (e.g., City of Cleburne v. Cleburne Living Center, Inc.) establishes that classifications based on physical disability or other non-suspect characteristics are not subject to heightened scrutiny. Drug addiction status is not analogous to race, national origin, gender, or religion.",
