      "claim": "Classifications that do not involve a suspect or quasi-suspect class and do not infringe on a fundamental right are subject to the rational basis test.",
      "evidence": "Standard constitutional law framework: If no fundamental right is infringed and no suspect class is involved, the government action is valid if it is rationally related to a legitimate state interest.",
      "weight": 0.25,
      "depends_on": [2]
